Package: tlosint-spiderfoot
Architecture: any
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, ${shlibs:Depends}, python3
Description: open source intelligence automation platform
 SpiderFoot automates OSINT collection against an IP address, domain name,
 hostname, network subnet, ASN, e-mail address or person's name. It queries
 over 200 data sources and correlates the results into a single graph of
 entities and relationships.
 .
 Two entry points are on PATH. "spiderfoot" starts the CherryPy web user
 interface, by default on 127.0.0.1:5001; nothing is started automatically,
 because this package deliberately ships no systemd unit -- whether an OSINT
 workstation runs a listening service is an operator decision, not a
 packaging one. "sfcli" is the command line client for an already running
 server. "sf.py" is a compatibility alias for "spiderfoot", because upstream's
 own tooling and documentation refer to the tool by that name.
 .
 Ships a self-contained virtualenv under /opt/tracelabs/spiderfoot so its
 dependency pins cannot collide with other OSINT tools on the system.
 .
 Upstream ships no setup.py and no pyproject.toml, so the tool itself cannot
 be pip-installed. The virtualenv holds only the pinned dependencies; the
 upstream source tree is laid down verbatim beside it and reached through
 small wrappers on PATH. See debian/upstream.pin for the pinning scheme and
 debian/README.Debian for the dependency relaxation this package carries.
